<!--/Post: 10774-->
<!--Post: 10810--><!--Time: 1110236751-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 3:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO, The inmates who sleep like babies are the ones who were afraid of getting caught. Once it&#39;s over and done with and they&#39;re in custody they no longer have to watch their backs &#40;as far as the law is concerned&#41;. They tire from being on the run. <BR> <BR>In Dennis Raders case, it&#39;s different. He never thought he would be found out. He thought he was too smart for that. I believe that he truly is depressed. He&#39;s depressed because his game has come to an end. Also, he&#39;s depressed because he lost his family and he knows it. They were  probably the only thing that really mattered to him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10810-->
<!--Post: 10813--><!--Time: 1110237824-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10813"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 3:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He thinks that it&#39;s tough to sleep now--just wait until prison.  I hope he can remember to sleep w/ his back against the wall &amp; w/ one eye open.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10813-->
<!--Post: 10838--><!--Time: 1110248621-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10838"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 6:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps he can find a hairy man to spoon with.  That may help him sleep.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
